ANACREON 10
"Reconstruction: 4021"
0     ; random scenario
1 3   ; 1-3 players
21    ; 21x21 galaxy
50    ; 50 planets
0     ; Difficulty: Beginner
50 0  ; 50+ years
4021
BEGINTEXT

        "...When the First Empire finally collapsed, the spasms and
   convultions of its death were so violent that the galaxy was thrown
   into a dark age that lasted nearly a thousand years.  Hundreds of worlds
   were devastated by the great wars at the end of the era.  Many more
   simply stagnated and decayed as they lost contact with Earth.  In the
   end, what was once a cohesive and monolithic unit spanning the stars
   of known space, degenerated into a dozen loose kingdoms trying to 
   maintain control over their own territories.  As the dark ages pro-
   gressed, even these kingdoms disappeared.  Entire worlds lost the
   technology to travel across the stars.  World by world the galaxy
   regressed thousands of years in the history of humanity..."
                                 From: The Seeds of Panemonde,
                                       by Lord Jonathan R. Rowehin.

 It is four thousand years after the collapse of the First Empire.  Although 
 not fully recovered from the cataclysm, the galaxy is slowly beginning to 
 unite once again.  Worlds have formed federations and federations have 
 turned into empires.  And although hundreds of worlds are still living 
 unaware that other humans inhabit the stars, there is a renewed hope in the 
 galaxy that a Second Empire will rise out of the first. 
NEWPAGE
 In this scenario, you will start out as the totalitarian ruler of a single
 earth-like world.  For the past few years your world has been building up
 its starfleet, preparing to forge an empire out of the surrounding worlds.
 Though not as technologically advanced as the First Empire, you possess a
 few ancient ships, remanents of another era, that will help you in your
 conquests.  Your ultimate goal is the unification of the galaxy,
 preferably under your flag.
ENDTEXT

; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Zone 2 is in the center of the galaxy and will contain mostly primitive
; planets.  Zones 3 through 6 form the periphery and will contain most of the
; powerful and advanced planets.
; Zones 7 through 11 will contain each of the 5 player empires and are spread
; throughout the galaxy.

; Define zone 2 in the center of the galaxy ------------------------------------
DefineZone 2 6,6 16,16

; Define zones 3-6 in the periphery --------------------------------------------
DefineZone 3  6,1  21,5
DefineZone 4 17,6  21,21
DefineZone 5  1,17 16,21
DefineZone 6  1,1   5,16
DefineZone 7  5,14  9,18            ; location of empire 1
DefineZone 8  13,4  17,8            ; location of empire 2
DefineZone 9  10,10 12,12           ; location of empire 3
DefineZone 10 16,16 20,20           ; location of empire 4
DefineZone 11  2,2   6,6            ; location of empire 5

; Create 5 player empires ------------------------------------------------------
; Each of the five empires has one of the previously created capitals.
; NOTE: If there are less than five players, then not all five empires will
; be created.  The capitals will remain as independent worlds, however.

CreatePlayerEmpire 0 0 7 0
CreatePlayerEmpire 1 0 7 0
CreatePlayerEmpire 2 0 7 0

CreateNPEmpire 1
3           ; Aggressor Empire
RndName     ; Name of the empire
0           ; (undefined)
7           ; Bio tech
0           ; (undefined)

CreateNPEmpire 2
3           ; Aggressor Empire
RndName     ; Name of the empire
0           ; (undefined)
7           ; Bio tech
0           ; (undefined)

CreateNPEmpire 3
3           ; Aggressor Empire
RndName     ; Name of the empire
0           ; (undefined)
7           ; Bio tech
0           ; (undefined)

CreateNPEmpire 4
3           ; Aggressor Empire
RndName     ; Name of the empire
0           ; (undefined)
7           ; Bio tech
0           ; (undefined)


